    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "opt-in per-table hlc mode (context.server.tables.todos.conflict_mode = \"hlc\"): conflicts resolve by the mutation ORIGIN Hybrid Logical Clock, not server arrival, so the outcome is deterministic regardless of which device reconnects first (the origin-order extension of the arrival-order default, P:verdict-completeness-transforms-and-conflict-rejection).",
      "arrival order would have let title-from-b win: this client pushed it AFTER device-b’s title-from-a had already arrived (seq 2), so a last-arrival-wins arbiter would overwrite title-from-a.",
      "HLC origin-order makes title-from-a win instead: the title column’s high-water-mark is H3 (2026-01-01T00:00:03, device-b) and the push carries H2 (2026-01-01T00:00:02, this client); H2 < H3, so every masked column loses and the whole mutation is SUPERSEDED, reverted to the HLC winner title-from-a, deterministically and independent of arrival.",
      "remove-wins is unchanged (delete-wins gate fires first); pull, fencing, cursor and delivery are all unchanged: hlc mode changes ONLY the push apply-decision."
    ],
